<i>Picking up transmission.</i>

278
00:24:11,650 --> 00:24:13,743
<i>[Whoosh]</i>

279
00:24:13,852 --> 00:24:16,821
[Chattering]

280
00:24:28,934 --> 00:24:30,663
<i>[Whoosh]</i>

281
00:24:54,392 --> 00:24:56,758
Who is this?

282
00:24:56,895 --> 00:24:58,829
<i>[Whoosh]</i>

283
00:25:16,181 --> 00:25:18,081
May I help you?

284
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:20,708
Yeah, uh-

285
00:25:20,819 --> 00:25:24,255
Hi, Mrs. Harris.
It's me, David.

286
00:25:24,356 --> 00:25:27,382
David?
David Rice?

287
00:25:27,492 --> 00:25:29,585
Millie was right.
You're not-

288
00:25:29,694 --> 00:25:32,254
Dead. Yeah.
No, I'm not.

289
00:25:32,364 --> 00:25:34,662
[Gasping, Laughing]

290
00:25:34,766 --> 00:25:37,860
Actually, I was hoping
you could tell me where to find Millie.

291
00:25:37,969 --> 00:25:41,336
Millie. She's got her own place
over on Morton.

292
00:25:41,439 --> 00:25:43,339
Number 260.

293
00:25:43,441 --> 00:25:45,500
- She's still here?
- Yeah, uh-huh.

294
00:25:45,610 --> 00:25:48,807
She works at Houlihan's Bar
down by the campus.

295
00:25:50,048 --> 00:25:51,913
- <i>##[Rock]</i>
- <i>[Man] That's it!</i>

296
00:25:52,017 --> 00:25:54,417
[Cheering, Chattering]

297
