00:34:32,637 --> 00:34:35,765
<i>[Man]</i>
<i>#If I don't say this now #

428
00:34:35,873 --> 00:34:38,865
<i>#I will surely break #

429
00:34:38,976 --> 00:34:41,877
<i>#As I'm meeting the world #

430
00:34:41,979 --> 00:34:44,106
<i>#I wanna say #

431
00:34:44,215 --> 00:34:47,241
<i>#Forget the urgency #

432
00:34:47,351 --> 00:34:50,286
<i>#But hurry up and wait #

433
00:34:50,388 --> 00:34:52,083
<i>#My heart has started #

434
00:34:52,190 --> 00:34:56,820
<i># To separate #

435
00:34:56,928 --> 00:35:00,022
<i>#Ohh-ohh, ohh-ohh #

436
00:35:00,131 --> 00:35:03,123
<i>#Please, baby #

437
00:35:03,234 --> 00:35:07,398
<i>#Oh-ohh, ohh-ohh #

438
00:35:09,273 --> 00:35:12,436
<i>#Ohh-ohh, ohh-ohh #

439
00:35:12,543 --> 00:35:14,738
- <i>#Please, baby #
- [Giggling]

440
00:35:14,846 --> 00:35:19,306
<i>#I'll look after you #

441
00:35:19,417 --> 00:35:21,647
I could eat.

442
00:35:21,752 --> 00:35:25,882
- <i>##[Continues]</i>
- You know, you could've just
asked me out on a date.

443
00:35:25,990 --> 00:35:28,015
<i>#So few come and go, girl #

444
00:35:28,126 --> 00:35:30,287
- <i># Will you, won't you #
- <i>[Bell Tolling]</i>

445
00:35:30,394 --> 00:35:33,420
<i>#Be the one</i>
<i>I'll always know #

446
00:35:33,531 --> 00:35:36,591
<i># When I'm losing my control #

447
00:35:36,701 --> 00:35:39,465
- <i>Grazie.</i>
- <i># This head spins around #

448
00:35:39,570 --> 00:35:42,300
<i># You're the only one</i>
<i>who knows #

449
00:35:42,406 --> 00:35:46,206
<i># This slowing sound #

450
00:35:46,310 --> 00:35:49,211
<i>#Ohh-ohh, ohh-ohh #

451
00:35:49,313 --> 00:35:53,079
- <i>##[Continues]</i>
- You know, this has always been
number one on my list.

452
00:35:53,184 --> 00:35:55,084
I know.

453
00:35:55,186 --> 00:35:58,314
You must be pretty good
at this, huh?

454
00:35:59,423 --> 00:36:01,391
Good at what?

455
00:36:01,492 --> 00:36:03,858
<i>#Please, baby #

456
00:36:03,961 --> 00:36:09,399
<i>#I'll look after you #

457
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:11,900
- <i>#Baby #
- Rookie.

458
00:36:12,003 --> 00:36:15,598
- <i>#Oh-ohh, ohh-ohh ##</i>
- No idea.

459
00:36:16,674 --> 00:36:18,437
<i>Whoa-whoa-whoa!</i>

460
00:36:18,543 --> 00:36:20,443
- W-W-W-W-Wait!
- Sorry, sir.

461
00:36:20,545 --> 00:36:23,446
- Sorry, sorry, sorry. No. No. It's impossible.
- What?

462
00:36:23,548 --> 00:36:27,575
- It's closed.
- What do you mean, it's closed? How is it closed?

463
00:36:27,685 --> 00:36:31,553
- We just wanna go inside there.
- No, it's impossible. No, no.

464
00:36:31,656 --> 00:36:34,284
- It's the Colosseum. How is it closed?
- It's impossible.

465
00:36:34,392 --> 00:36:38,385
<i>David, it's okay. I got to see it from outside.</i>
<i>That's good enough.</i>

466
00:36:38,496 --> 00:36:42,364
- You know, she came all this way to go inside.
- Hey, come on.

467
00:36:42,466 --> 00:36:44,400
Sorry, he's- I don't know.

468
00:36:44,502 --> 00:36:46,470
- <i>Ciao.</i>
- Bye.

469
00:36:48,172 --> 00:36:50,140
<i>[Whoosh]</i>

470
00:36:51,909 --> 00:36:53,809
<i>Millie!</i>

471
00:36:53,911 --> 00:36:55,970
- <i>Come on.</i>
- What?

472
00:36:56,080 --> 00:36:58,105
Come on.
How about a private tour?

473
00:36:58,216 --> 00:37:01,276
It's closed. We can't
break into the Colosseum.

474
00:37:01,385 --> 00:37:04,843
Who said it's closed?
The door was open.

475
00:37:04,956 --> 00:37:06,924
Wanna see the Colosseum or not?

476
00:37:09,193 --> 00:37:11,161
Come on.

477
00:37:11,262 --> 00:37:13,730
We so should not be doing this.

478
00:37:38,256 --> 00:37:40,224
<i>[Millie]</i>
<i>This place is amazing.</i>

479
00:37:40,324 --> 00:37:42,315
<i>[David]</i>
<i>I wanted you to see this.</i>

480
00:37:42,426 --> 00:37:45,224
You've gotta admit,
it's worth the risk.

481
00:37:46,264 --> 00:37:48,232
Yeah.

482
00:37:54,171 --> 00:37:56,639
- [Laughing] It's so cool!
- It is.

483
00:38:02,146 --> 00:38:06,810
Down here is where they used to keep
the gladiators and the lions in cages?

484
00:38:06,917 --> 00:38:10,478
- We should go down there.
- Can't go down there. It's off-limits.

485
00:38:10,588 --> 00:38:13,182
- Even when it's open.
- Nothing's off-limits.

486
00:38:13,291 --> 00:38:15,054
What?

487
00:38:15,159 --> 00:38:16,888
- [Scoffs]
- <i>[Whoosh]</i>

488
00:38:19,830 --> 00:38:21,559
Psst! Millie!

489
00:38:24,802 --> 00:38:27,498
Did that door just open too?

490
00:38:27,605 --> 00:38:29,539
- It's open now.
- Yeah.

491
00:38:29,640 --> 00:38:33,406
You're gonna want to see this.
Trust me.

492
00:38:39,650 --> 00:38:41,618
<i>[Door Closes]</i>

493
00:38:48,125 --> 00:38:50,093
<i>Bet you that's worth something.</i>

494
00:38:50,194 --> 00:38:52,492
<i>[Laughs]</i>
<i>Maybe.</i>

495
00:38:58,736 --> 00:39:02,365
[Chuckles]
Uh-oh.

496
00:39:02,473 --> 00:39:04,600
I think he's telling you
do not enter.

497
00:39:06,177 --> 00:39:08,805
You speak Italian?

498
00:39:08,913 --> 00:39:10,813
No.

499
00:39:10,915 --> 00:39:12,815
- Well, uh, <i>I'ingresso...</i>
- Uh-huh?

500
00:39:12,917 --> 00:39:14,817
means "come on in."

501
00:39:14,919 --> 00:39:18,150
Oh! I thought it meant "bullshit."

502
00:39:18,255 --> 00:39:21,156
Well, no, that means that you should
stay here while I go around...

503
00:39:21,258 --> 00:39:23,658
and open it from the other side.

504
00:39:23,761 --> 00:39:25,661
It's all right.
You'll catch on.

505
00:39:25,763 --> 00:39:27,731
Mmm.

506
00:39:31,268 --> 00:39:33,236
[Giggles]

507
00:39:39,343 --> 00:39:42,938
Thank you very much.
Next showing will be at 6:00.

508
00:39:43,047 --> 00:39:46,107
Don't forget to tip your usher.

509
00:39:47,585 --> 00:39:49,849
- <i>Oh, uh-</i>
- Uh, do you mind, man?

510
00:39:49,954 --> 00:39:52,514
- Whoa!
- Just a little privacy, eh?

511
00:39:52,623 --> 00:39:54,181
- Sorry, man.
- <i>Big Colosseum. Guy peein'?</i>

512
00:39:54,291 --> 00:39:57,749
This isn't a fashion show.
I'm taking a piss. Do you mind?

513
00:39:59,463 --> 00:40:01,590
Place is all yours.

514
00:40:03,734 --> 00:40:05,634
[Shouts]

515
00:40:05,736 --> 00:40:09,934
Wouldn't open that door if I were you,
not if I wanted my girlfriend to keep breathing.

516
00:40:10,040 --> 00:40:13,601
<i>What are you gonna do anyway?</i>
<i>Bring her down, have a nice, romantic picnic?</i>

517
00:40:13,711 --> 00:40:16,612
Nice little tea party?
Is that what you think is gonna happen?

518
00:40:16,714 --> 00:40:19,478
- If you so much as look at her wrong-
- You gonna jump me? Where?

519
00:40:21,819 --> 00:40:24,788
Did you think you were the only one?

520
00:40:26,323 --> 00:40:28,382
You really have no idea, do you?

521
00:40:28,492 --> 00:40:30,392
You lead the life you live.

522
00:40:30,494 --> 00:40:33,327
<i>You think you can just go on a little</i>
<i>Roman holiday and they wouldn't notice?</i>

523
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:35,331
Just jump
all over the place-

524
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:37,333
jump, jump, jump,
jump, jump, jump-

525
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:39,403
and nothing's gonna happen?

526
00:40:40,771 --> 00:40:43,171
Well, they've noticed.

527
00:40:43,274 --> 00:40:44,901
Not me.

528
00:40:45,009 --> 00:40:47,671
I mean I already knew.
I'm not talking about me, but them.

529
00:40:47,778 --> 00:40:49,746
Down there.

530
00:40:53,117 --> 00:40:55,085
Hello, boys.

531
00:40:58,522 --> 00:41:00,490
Just me, then.

532
00:41:00,591 --> 00:41:04,049
- [High-pitched Charging]
- Huh. That's new.

533
00:41:06,530 --> 00:41:09,931
[Grunting, Groaning]

534
00:41:16,273 --> 00:41:18,241
Welcome to the war.

535
00:41:33,057 --> 00:41:35,355
Just let me know if you guys
are gettin' tired.

536
00:41:36,894 --> 00:41:39,362
- Close.
- David?

537
00:41:41,899 --> 00:41:44,367
- [Screams]
- What's going on?

538
00:41:44,468 --> 00:41:46,629
[Panting]

539
00:41:49,106 --> 00:41:51,199
Great. Let's meet
the girlfriend, shall we?

540
00:41:51,308 --> 00:41:53,367
No.

541
00:42:04,922 --> 00:42:08,323
- [Grunts]
- Who are these people?

542
00:42:08,425 --> 00:42:10,325
Paladins.
Paladins kill Jumpers.

543
00:42:10,427 --> 00:42:12,224
I kill Paladins.
Class dismissed.

544
00:42:14,131 --> 00:42:17,658
<i>[Woman Speaking Italian]</i>

545
00:42:17,768 --> 00:42:20,236
<i>Polizia! Polizia!</i>

546
00:42:20,337 --> 00:42:21,998
- <i>Polizia!</i>
- Uh-oh.

547
00:42:23,774 --> 00:42:25,571
Wait!

548
00:42:32,716 --> 00:42:34,809
I just came through your jump scar.

549
00:42:34,919 --> 00:42:37,820
What do you think
you're doing here? Huh?

550
00:42:37,922 --> 00:42:40,322
If I were you, I'd jump right back.

551
00:42:40,424 --> 00:42:43,154
You're not supposed to see
all this stuff. Get out!

552
00:42:45,195 --> 00:42:49,928
So if you'd like to
kindly fuck off, as in now.

553
00:42:50,034 --> 00:42:52,468
Maybe your girlfriend's still alive.

554
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:54,538
[Gasps]

555
00:42:55,673 --> 00:42:57,368
- Hey.
- Hey.

556
00:42:58,509 --> 00:43:01,034
- What happened to you?
- Uh, nothing.

557
00:43:01,145 --> 00:43:04,273
Let's go. Come on.
I think we should just get out of here.

558
00:43:04,381 --> 00:43:06,611
<i>[Millie]</i>
<i>That didn't sound like nothing.</i>

559
00:43:06,717 --> 00:43:10,448
You were right. Okay? I shouldn't have
gone down there. Everything's fine.

560
00:43:10,554 --> 00:43:13,546
Come on. We can
still make the museum.

561
00:43:14,658 --> 00:43:17,559
<i>[Sirens Wailing]</i>

562
00:43:19,063 --> 00:43:20,963
- <i>[Woman Speaking Italian]</i>
- <i>David?</i>

563
00:43:21,065 --> 00:43:22,965
<i>Will you talk to me?</i>
<i>Please?</i>

564
00:43:23,067 --> 00:43:24,967
Must be a cab around here somewhere.

565
00:43:25,069 --> 00:43:27,469
Why aren't you talking to me?
Please talk to me.

566
00:43:27,571 --> 00:43:30,972
- I'll tell you everything back at the hotel. Okay?
- I'm not waiting for the hotel.

567
00:43:31,075 --> 00:43:34,306
- Look, Millie, it's, uh- it's all fine. Okay?
- No, it's not all fine.

568
00:43:34,411 --> 00:43:37,676
- I wasn't supposed to go back there.
- <i>[Men Shouting In Italian]</i>

569
00:43:37,781 --> 00:43:40,978
- [Speaking Italian]
- Huh?

570
00:43:41,085 --> 00:43:42,985
Uh, <i>no comprende.</i>

571
00:43:43,087 --> 00:43:45,851
- [Italian]
- No, I think you guys made a mistake.

572
00:43:45,956 --> 00:43:48,481
- Be quiet.
- You're looking for that guy over there.

573
00:43:48,592 --> 00:43:52,756
- [Italian]
- I'm sorry. I know I wasn't
supposed to be back there.

574
00:43:52,863 --> 00:43:54,763
<i>[All Shouting]</i>

575
00:43:54,865 --> 00:43:56,992
<i>Calma, calma, calma, calma.</i>

576
00:43:57,101 --> 00:43:59,729
Can't you just let us off with a warning-
Whoa! Okay, okay.

577
00:43:59,837 --> 00:44:02,067
- [Italian]
- Okay, okay, okay.

578
00:44:02,172 --> 00:44:05,266
- Millie, just go back to the hotel. Okay?
- No-

579
00:44:05,376 --> 00:44:08,345
- <i>No, no, we're not together.</i>
- I'm with him!

580
00:44:08,445 --> 00:44:10,743
I don't know her.
Millie, go back to the hotel.

581
00:44:10,848 --> 00:44:14,249
- No. No.
- [Siren Wailing]

582
00:44:15,953 --> 00:44:19,184
I told you.
I want to see Millie.

583
00:44:19,289 --> 00:44:22,554
- Where is the body?
- I didn't do anything, okay?

584
00:44:22,660 --> 00:44:25,686
I-I don't know how many times
you want me to tell you the same thing.

585
00:44:29,833 --> 00:44:32,028
Do you know how much longer
he's gonna be back there?

586
00:44:32,136 --> 00:44:34,104
We wait for <i>magistrato.</i>

587
00:44:34,204 --> 00:44:37,230
Yeah. I know. We've been waiting for
a <i>magistrato</i> all night.

588
00:44:38,876 --> 00:44:41,606
[Speaking Italian]

589
00:44:41,712 --> 00:44:43,942
I don't speak your-
I don't know what you're saying.

590
00:44:44,048 --> 00:44:46,107
Now you "seat," or we seat you.

591
00:44:46,216 --> 00:44:48,207
- Okay.
- Seat!

592
00:44:48,318 --> 00:44:50,445
I seat.

593
00:44:50,554 --> 00:44:52,647
- <i>[David] She's got nothing to do with this.</i>
- [Speaking Italian]

594
00:44:52,756 --> 00:44:54,656
<i>[Italian]</i>

595
00:44:54,758 --> 00:44:56,658
[Italian]

596
00:44:56,760 --> 00:45:00,924
<i>Allora,</i> the magistrate is here.
We will hold on to your passport.

597
00:45:01,031 --> 00:45:04,125
<i>Don't worry.</i>
<i>You won't need it where you're going.</i>

598
00:45:05,235 --> 00:45:07,635
<i>[Chattering In Italian]</i>

599
00:45:16,380 --> 00:45:18,439
Hello, David.

600
00:45:18,549 --> 00:45:22,007
<i>You've only got about 30 seconds before</i>
<i>they come through that door. You understand?</i>

601
00:45:22,119 --> 00:45:24,087
You have to get out of here.

602
00:45:24,188 --> 00:45:26,918
- Ditch the girl. If she's with you, she's dead.
- <i>Mom.</i>

603
00:45:27,024 --> 00:45:29,925
- Mom.
- Twenty seconds, David.

604
00:45:31,462 --> 00:45:35,364
Mom! Mom!

605
00:45:35,466 --> 00:45:36,490
Hey!

606
00:45:36,600 --> 00:45:39,296
[Grunts]

607
00:45:39,403 --> 00:45:41,963
- <i>[Handcuffs Click]</i>
- [Whimpers]

608
00:45:50,314 --> 00:45:51,781
Millie.

609
00:45:53,117 --> 00:45:55,847
All done. You okay?

610
00:45:55,953 --> 00:45:57,921
Mm-hmm. Hey.

611
00:45:58,021 --> 00:46:00,819
- I'm free to walk.
- They just let you go?

612
00:46:00,924 --> 00:46:03,757
- They just let me go.
- Just like that?

613
00:46:03,861 --> 00:46:06,523
Just like that.
Come on.

614
00:46:07,898 --> 00:46:10,731
[Millie] If they just let you go,
why are we running?

615
00:46:10,834 --> 00:46:13,564
Well, uh, they really strongly suggested
that we leave town now.

616
00:46:13,670 --> 00:46:16,969
- But what did they say to you?
- Asked me some questions.

617
00:46:17,074 --> 00:46:20,134
- For eight hours?
- They had a lot of questions.

618
00:46:20,244 --> 00:46:22,678
I really want to trust you.
You're making it extremely difficult.

619
00:46:22,780 --> 00:46:24,680
All right. So trust me.
Let's go.

620
00:46:28,051 --> 00:46:30,019
Whoa!

621
00:46:31,255 --> 00:46:33,155
Whoa! Hey.

622
00:46:33,257 --> 00:46:36,055
- Can you take us? Yeah?
- <i>##[Car Radio: Rap]</i>

623
00:46:36,160 --> 00:46:39,357
Get in the cab, Millie.
Millie, get in the car.

624
00:46:39,463 --> 00:46:41,363
[Clears Throat]

625
00:46:41,465 --> 00:46:44,525
Please.
Please get in the cab.

626
00:46:44,635 --> 00:46:47,160
<i>##[Continues]</i>

627
00:46:50,207 --> 00:46:52,801
<i>[Chattering]</i>

628
00:46:52,910 --> 00:46:55,504
<i>[Woman On P.A.</i>
<i>Speaking Italian]</i>

629
00:47:12,095 --> 00:47:13,995
<i>That's yours.</i>

630
00:47:14,097 --> 00:47:16,565
Remember how I told you you didn't
need to tell me everything?

631
00:47:17,935 --> 00:47:19,903
I changed my mind.

632
00:47:25,008 --> 00:47:26,976
What's in the backpack?

633
00:47:51,134 --> 00:47:53,102
Where did you get that?

634
00:48:00,277 --> 00:48:02,370
I don't want to lie to you.

635
00:48:04,314 --> 00:48:07,613
But you don't want to
tell me the truth either.

636
00:48:11,221 --> 00:48:13,416
I can't get on this flight
with you, Millie.

637
00:48:13,523 --> 00:48:16,686
<i>This is as far as we go together.</i>

638
00:48:32,075 --> 00:48:34,908
- <i>[Woman] To Detroit?</i>
- Mm-hmm.

639
00:48:42,352 --> 00:48:43,649
<i>[Cell Phone Beeps]</i>

640
00:48:43,820 --> 00:48:44,980
<i>[Roland]</i>
<i>Roland.</i>

641
00:48:45,088 --> 00:48:47,056
[Man]
We lost him, sir.

642
00:48:48,191 --> 00:48:50,159
- How many did you send?
- Two men.

643
00:48:50,260 --> 00:48:53,252
- I told you to send everybody.
- Well, she said two would be enough...

644
00:48:53,363 --> 00:48:55,297
but, uh, they missed him.

645
00:48:55,399 --> 00:48:58,061
It's like he knew we were coming.

646
00:48:58,168 --> 00:49:00,966
We're searching the grid now.

647
00:49:01,071 --> 00:49:04,802
Keep me informed.
I'm taking a different tack.

648
00:49:15,519 --> 00:49:18,113
[Ignition Indicator Beeps]

649
00:49:18,221 --> 00:49:20,189
William Rice?

650
00:49:20,290 --> 00:49:21,780
Yeah.

651
00:49:21,892 --> 00:49:23,860
I.R.S.

652
00:49:25,128 --> 00:49:28,461
Could we, uh, go inside and talk?

653
00:49:30,634 --> 00:49:33,432
I don't have to ask.
That's a courtesy.

654
00:49:33,537 --> 00:49:36,768
- <i>[Chattering On TV]</i>
- So, what's this all about?

655
00:49:36,873 --> 00:49:39,034
Your son. David.

656
00:49:41,011 --> 00:49:44,105
Why? Is he in some kind
of trouble or something?

657
00:49:46,516 --> 00:49:50,316
This will go a lot swifter
if you let me ask the questions.

658
00:49:50,420 --> 00:49:53,321
When's the last time
you saw your son?

659
00:49:54,424 --> 00:49:56,892
Eight years ago.

660
00:49:59,396 --> 00:50:01,364
Eight years?

661
00:50:01,465 --> 00:50:03,433
That's right.

662
00:50:05,736 --> 00:50:08,068
What about friends?

663
00:50:08,171 --> 00:50:10,071
Anybody I can talk to?

664
00:50:10,173 --> 00:50:12,368
He didn't have
a whole lot of friends.

665
00:50:12,476 --> 00:50:15,138
I'd like to talk to
David's mother if I could.

666
00:50:15,245 --> 00:50:19,306
Yeah, me too.
If you find her, tell her I said hello.

667
00:50:19,416 --> 00:50:21,384
That her?

668
00:50:21,485 --> 00:50:23,646
Mary Rice. At least that was
her name back then.

669
00:50:28,125 --> 00:50:30,491
When's the last time you saw her?

670
00:50:30,594 --> 00:50:33,062
She split when the kid turned five.

671
00:50:33,163 --> 00:50:35,063
Five. Oh.

672
00:50:35,165 --> 00:50:37,258
<i>Haven't heard a word since.</i>

673
00:50:43,707 --> 00:50:46,835
If I hear anything,
I'll be sure to give you a holler.

674
00:50:49,212 --> 00:50:51,942
<i>[Door Closes]</i>

675
00:50:52,049 --> 00:50:55,041
- No, you won't.
- No. I won't.

676
00:50:58,288 --> 00:51:00,882
Have you seen the special move
you can do on this new thing?

677
00:51:00,991 --> 00:51:05,519
They've added this new control and, like,
you just- If you-Just double-click it. See that?

678
00:51:05,629 --> 00:51:07,529
What do you say?
Whoa.

679
00:51:07,631 --> 00:51:10,065
<i>[Whoosh]</i>

680
00:51:10,167 --> 00:51:12,101
Still alive, are ya?

681
00:51:12,202 --> 00:51:15,262
<i>[TV: Video Game</i>
<i>Machine Gun Fire]</i>

682
00:51:17,908 --> 00:51:20,604
- <i>[Man On TV] I'm hit!</i>
- <i>[Man #2 On TV] He's dead.</i>

683
00:51:20,710 --> 00:51:23,645
- What? That's just great.
- There's more of them?

684
00:51:23,747 --> 00:51:27,808
<i>Hundreds more. I'm tracking 10 right now.</i>
<i>What do you care? There's lots more.</i>

685
00:51:27,918 --> 00:51:30,648
- What about the rest?
- What about the rest?

686
00:51:30,754 --> 00:51:32,813
Like I said, I hunt them.

687
00:51:32,923 --> 00:51:34,891
- <i>Start again.</i>
- So who are these guys?

688
00:51:34,991 --> 00:51:36,720
I told you.
They're Paladins.

689
00:51:36,827 --> 00:51:40,422
Yeah, you told me their name.
You didn't tell me what they want.

690
00:51:40,530 --> 00:51:43,988
- <i>[Machine Gun Fire On TV]</i>
- Well, it's pretty simple,
isn't it? They want us dead.

691
00:51:44,101 --> 00:51:47,229
- Didn't you figure that out yet?
- [Chuckles] Yeah. No, I got that much.

692
00:51:47,337 --> 00:51:49,237
- Good. I'm glad.
- Yeah. Thanks.

693
00:51:49,339 --> 00:51:51,273
- Do you mind just, uh-
- Why?

694
00:51:51,374 --> 00:51:53,274
Because we can do
whatever the hell we want.

695
00:51:53,376 --> 00:51:55,276
- Now can you please just-
- I'm hit!

696
00:51:55,378 --> 00:51:58,677
- He's dead.
- Great. Thanks.

697
00:51:58,782 --> 00:52:01,012
You really don't get it, do you?

698
00:52:01,118 --> 00:52:04,110
Paladins have been killing
Jumpers for years.

699
00:52:04,221 --> 00:52:06,121
Way back since medieval times.

700
00:52:07,424 --> 00:52:09,517
They're fanatics.
Religious nut jobs.

701
00:52:09,626 --> 00:52:12,356
Inquisition. Witch hunts.
That was them.

702
00:52:12,462 --> 00:52:16,421
Look. They're smart.
They're fast. They're organized.

703
00:52:16,533 --> 00:52:18,967
No matter what, they'll kill anyone
that gets in their way.

704
00:52:19,069 --> 00:52:22,869
Like your family.
Your friends.

705
00:52:22,973 --> 00:52:26,704
That little girlfriend
you're traipsing around Rome with you.

706
00:52:26,810 --> 00:52:31,042
They're dead.
All of 'em.

707
00:52:31,148 --> 00:52:33,742
Get used to it.
It's just a matter of time.

708
00:52:37,020 --> 00:52:39,648
I'm gonna get some takeaway.
Do you want some?

709
00:52:39,756 --> 00:52:41,656
<i>[Whoosh]</i>

710
00:52:41,758 --> 00:52:44,352
<i>[Airplane Engine Roaring]</i>

711
00:52:48,798 --> 00:52:50,789
<i>[Chattering]</i>

712
00:53:00,076 --> 00:53:02,044
<i>[Chattering On TV]</i>

713
00:53:02,145 --> 00:53:04,113
[Hinges Squeak]

714
00:53:06,183 --> 00:53:08,151
<i>[Chattering Continues]</i>

715
00:53:12,589 --> 00:53:14,250
He's your father.

716
00:53:14,357 --> 00:53:17,417
I'm sorry. I talked to him,
but he wouldn't budge.

717
00:53:17,527 --> 00:53:21,054
<i>He can be so stubborn.</i>
<i>I don't know how my mother puts up with him.</i>

718
00:53:35,278 --> 00:53:37,405
Somebody get some help!

719
00:53:39,182 --> 00:53:41,343
- Now!
- <i>[Man] What happened?</i>

720
00:53:41,451 --> 00:53:43,851
- <i>[Woman] What's going on in here?</i>
- <i>[Chattering]</i>

721
00:53:46,790 --> 00:53:48,519
- <i>[Man] Get the paddles.</i>
- <i>[Shouting]</i>

722
00:53:48,625 --> 00:53:50,559
<i>[Chattering]</i>

723
00:53:52,596 --> 00:53:54,894
You okay? Stay still.

724
00:53:57,500 --> 00:53:59,468
<i>[Man]</i>
<i>I'm not getting a pulse.</i>

725
00:54:02,172 --> 00:54:04,140
<i>What the hell happened here?</i>

726
00:54:07,210 --> 00:54:09,110
Oh!

727
00:54:10,146 --> 00:54:11,943
- <i>[Whoosh]</i>
- Mark.

728
00:54:12,048 --> 00:54:14,482
- Jesus Christ.
- What did you tell him?

729
00:54:14,584 --> 00:54:16,575
- How did they know about Ann Arbor?
- Don't touch me.

730
00:54:16,686 --> 00:54:19,348
- Who'd you tell?
- Stay the hell away from me.

731
00:54:19,456 --> 00:54:22,482
Was it a black guy with white hair?
Was his name Roland?

732
00:54:22,592 --> 00:54:24,492
Just answer the question...

733
00:54:24,594 --> 00:54:26,789
or I'll drop you off the top
of Mount Everest, okay?

734
00:54:26,896 --> 00:54:28,796
- What? What?
- What did you tell him?

735
00:54:28,898 --> 00:54:31,230
I don't-What? Tell what?

736
00:54:31,334 --> 00:54:33,234
I know you told him
about home, all right?

737
00:54:33,336 --> 00:54:36,203
I know you told him about Ann Arbor.
Did you tell him about Millie?

738
00:54:36,306 --> 00:54:37,967
I told him everything.

739
00:54:38,074 --> 00:54:40,304
Why?
Why did you do that?

740
00:54:40,410 --> 00:54:42,708
- Why not?
- [Shouts]

741
00:54:42,812 --> 00:54:44,746
<i>Who are you?</i>

742
00:54:45,915 --> 00:54:47,883
<i>[Wind Howling]</i>

743
00:54:51,454 --> 00:54:53,581
Whoa! Whew!

744
00:54:53,690 --> 00:54:55,590
Where'd the Paladin go?

745
00:54:55,692 --> 00:54:58,160
- Swimming.
- Pacific?

746
00:54:58,261 --> 00:55:01,856
No. Actually, Atlantic.
Nice little shark pit round Cuba.

747
00:55:03,633 --> 00:55:05,863
<i>Uh, what do you think you're doing?</i>

748
00:55:05,969 --> 00:55:08,437
- Put that stuff back!
- Actually, I need to borrow a few things.

749
00:55:08,538 --> 00:55:10,870
Just stay away from the wall!

750
00:55:10,974 --> 00:55:12,441
I'll cut your eyes out.

751
00:55:12,542 --> 00:55:14,976
[Grunts]
I need to find Roland.

752
00:55:15,078 --> 00:55:17,410
No, you don't.
No, you don't.

753
00:55:17,514 --> 00:55:19,573
- I only got eight hours.
- Eight hours?

754
00:55:19,683 --> 00:55:21,617
There's a girl-
Her flight lands in eight hours.

755
00:55:21,718 --> 00:55:23,515
Think that stuff's gonna help?
That stuff's four years old.

756
00:55:23,620 --> 00:55:26,384
<i>Do you want me to jump you back to</i>
<i>high school so you can learn something?</i>

757
00:55:26,489 --> 00:55:29,390
I've been tracking him for 10 years.
Look at this. Look.

758
00:55:31,594 --> 00:55:34,859
You see this?
Our first round in Nepal.

759
00:55:34,964 --> 00:55:37,194
You should see the one he gave me
back in Prague.

760
00:55:37,300 --> 00:55:40,064
Look. Forget it.
Forget Roland.

761
00:55:40,170 --> 00:55:42,138
Don't waste your time.

762
00:55:42,238 --> 00:55:44,297
Just leave it to me.

763
00:55:56,419 --> 00:55:58,387
- Do you mind?
- Look.

764
00:55:58,488 --> 00:56:00,581
Little, uh- Little privacy here?

765
00:56:00,690 --> 00:56:03,090
You know, this is
kind of my thing. Just-

766
00:56:03,193 --> 00:56:06,788
Just- Get-You know, turn around.

767
00:56:06,896 --> 00:56:08,864
Yeah.

768
00:56:08,965 --> 00:56:13,265
I'm- I was thinking
that if we do this together...

769
00:56:13,370 --> 00:56:15,270
we could get him.

770
00:56:15,372 --> 00:56:17,465
What? You mean, like, you and me?

771
00:56:17,574 --> 00:56:20,099
- <i>Yeah.</i>
- Like we team up?

772
00:56:20,210 --> 00:56:22,872
- Yeah.
- [Chuckles]

773
00:56:22,979 --> 00:56:25,470
Look. I'm sorry,
but I don't play well with others.

774
00:56:41,398 --> 00:56:44,890
<i>Do me a favor, yeah?</i>
<i>Don't be here when I get back.</i>

775
00:56:45,001 --> 00:56:47,663
Find a rock. Crawl under it.
Stay there.

776
00:56:56,212 --> 00:56:58,737
<i>Joi woo,</i> brother.

777
00:56:58,848 --> 00:57:01,316
That's "good-bye" in Chinese.

778
00:57:14,364 --> 00:57:16,332
<i>[Chattering]</i>

779
00:57:20,203 --> 00:57:23,172
<i>[People Arguing In Japanese]</i>

780
00:57:27,944 --> 00:57:31,209
Yeah. No. I've been meaning to call.
Really. I still really want to get the tattoo.

781
00:57:31,314 --> 00:57:32,804
[Japanese]

782
00:57:37,520 --> 00:57:40,182
[Horn Honks]

783
00:57:43,193 --> 00:57:45,320
- [Horn Honks]
- [Man Shouts In Japanese]

784
00:57:55,171 --> 00:57:57,139
<i>[Whoosh]</i>

785
00:58:07,016 --> 00:58:08,984
You can't keep following me.

786
00:58:09,085 --> 00:58:11,815
<i>Actually-[Clears Throat]</i>
<i>I'm the one person who can.</i>

787
00:58:11,921 --> 00:58:13,821
Yeah, lucky me.

788
00:58:15,158 --> 00:58:17,251
<i>[Horns Honking]</i>

789
00:58:27,103 --> 00:58:29,401
Why are you walking?

790
00:58:29,506 --> 00:58:32,805
I mean, l- I know Tokyo pretty well.
I got a lot of jump sites here.

791
00:58:32,909 --> 00:58:37,676
You know, l-l- I like walking for a change.
Makes me feel normal.

792
00:58:37,780 --> 00:58:40,908
You, uh-You ever read
Marvel Team-up?

793
00:58:41,017 --> 00:58:42,917
Yeah, I read it. And?

794
00:58:43,019 --> 00:58:47,718
Two superheroes joining forces
for, like, uh, a limited run.

795
00:58:47,824 --> 00:58:50,793
I see what you're trying to do, yeah?
I'm not buying it.

796
00:58:50,894 --> 00:58:54,295
For your own sake, just go home.

797
00:58:54,397 --> 00:58:57,195
- You live in a cave.
- It's called a lair.

798
00:58:57,300 --> 00:58:59,268
And what's the point?

799
00:58:59,369 --> 00:59:03,465
I'm just saying, you know.
We, uh, kind of have this common thing.

800
00:59:05,808 --> 00:59:07,799
And I know where to find Roland.

801
00:59:10,914 --> 00:59:12,905
<i>[Chattering]</i>

802
00:59:19,355 --> 00:59:21,323
[David]
So we doing this, or what?

803
00:59:30,567 --> 00:59:32,535
<i>[Engine Starts]</i>

804
00:59:37,407 --> 00:59:40,171
<i>Whoo!</i>

805
00:59:48,518 --> 00:59:50,543
Sorry. Clutch stuck.

806
00:59:52,388 --> 00:59:55,380
- You're real subtle.
- Yeah, I'm not gonna get rid of you, am I?

807
00:59:59,295 --> 01:00:02,025
[Horns Honking]

808
01:00:12,275 --> 01:00:13,435
Whoa. Whoa.

809
01:00:13,543 --> 01:00:15,841
You might want to hold on, son.

810
01:00:17,547 --> 01:00:18,605
[Screams]

811
01:00:27,924 --> 01:00:30,484
<i>[Horns Honking]</i>

812
01:00:32,295 --> 01:00:34,422
That was close.

813
01:00:34,530 --> 01:00:37,192
Not bad.

814
01:00:37,300 --> 01:00:40,497
This thing must be two tons, easy.
How are you, uh-

815
01:00:40,603 --> 01:00:42,901
If it moves, I can jump it.

816
01:00:43,006 --> 01:00:46,305
<i>Actually, I knew this Jumper once-</i>
<i>crazy bastard-</i>

817
01:00:46,409 --> 01:00:48,673
tried to hop a whole building.
[Chuckles]

818
01:00:48,778 --> 01:00:51,212
- Won't be trying that again.
- Why's that?

819
01:00:51,314 --> 01:00:53,805
That's 'cause he's dead.
Killed him.

820
01:00:53,916 --> 01:00:57,477
Still managed to shake it
a little though.

821
01:01:01,190 --> 01:01:03,590
<i>So how long you been doing this for?</i>

822
01:01:03,693 --> 01:01:06,355
- Doing what? Driving?
- No. Jumping.

823
01:01:06,462 --> 01:01:08,396
- <i>[Radio Channels Changing]</i>
- Since I was five.

824
01:01:08,498 --> 01:01:10,398
- Five?
- Yeah.

825
01:01:10,500 --> 01:01:13,901
- <i>##[Radio: Rock]</i>
- How'd you keep it a secret from people?

826
01:01:14,003 --> 01:01:17,370
- <i>Like your parents.</i>
- It's pretty easy when they're not around.

827
01:01:17,473 --> 01:01:19,737
- <i>##[Radio: Heavy Metal]</i>
- Where were they?

828
01:01:19,842 --> 01:01:21,810
Not around.

829
01:01:26,215 --> 01:01:29,207
You know, my mom-
she took off when I was five.

830
01:01:30,820 --> 01:01:33,050
<i>I know what it's like</i>
<i>to not, you know-</i>

831
01:01:33,156 --> 01:01:35,590
My dad, he-

832
01:01:35,692 --> 01:01:38,058
Did I ask about your family?

833
01:01:39,295 --> 01:01:42,287
I mean, are we on
<i>Oprah</i> here or-

834
01:01:45,368 --> 01:01:48,462
- <i>##[Heavy Metal]</i>
- <i>#Do you want it</i>
<i>Do you need it #

835
01:01:48,571 --> 01:01:51,062
<i>#Let me hear it</i>
<i>Ladies and gentlemen ##</i>

836
01:01:51,174 --> 01:01:53,972
<i>[David]</i>
<i>Griffin, I can't keep doing this. I gotta go.</i>

837
01:01:54,077 --> 01:01:56,841
Her flight lands any second.
I need an answer.

838
01:01:58,181 --> 01:01:59,808
- [Horn Honks]
- [Man Shouts]

839
01:01:59,916 --> 01:02:04,046
This is it, all right?
Marvel Team-up, now or never.

840
01:02:04,153 --> 01:02:07,782
- [Horn Honks]
- A very limited run, right?

841
01:02:07,890 --> 01:02:10,882
Save her, kill him, you know.
We're done.

842
01:02:10,993 --> 01:02:13,461
All right, Spidey.

843
01:02:15,364 --> 01:02:17,264
Hey!

844
01:02:17,433 --> 01:02:19,526
<i>[Man On P.A.]</i>
<i>Due to increased security measures, all bags-</i>

845
01:02:19,635 --> 01:02:22,866
- Hey!
- <i>Detroit International Airport asks you...</i>

846
01:02:22,972 --> 01:02:24,997
<i>to keep your bags in your</i>
<i>possession at all times.</i>

847
01:02:25,108 --> 01:02:29,511
<i>[Woman On P.A.] Flight 427 to Cleveland</i>
<i>will now be boarding at Gate Number 5.</i>

848
01:02:30,847 --> 01:02:34,613
- Hey.
- The flight from Rome landed an hour ago.

849
01:02:34,717 --> 01:02:36,685
Oh, no.

850
01:02:37,720 --> 01:02:41,486
<i>You didn't check on the flight?</i>

851
01:02:41,591 --> 01:02:43,957
All right. Well, we gotta find her,
you know.

852
01:02:44,060 --> 01:02:47,086
You go find her. I'm gonna arm up.
Meet me back at the lair.

853
01:02:47,196 --> 01:02:49,096
- All right?
- Fine.

854
01:02:49,198 --> 01:02:50,165
[Gasps]

855
01:02:50,266 --> 01:02:52,598
<i>[Woman On P.A., Indistinct]</i>

856
01:02:52,702 --> 01:02:54,602
What you looking at?

857
01:02:58,608 --> 01:03:00,508
Boo!

858
01:03:04,614 --> 01:03:09,517
Hey. Uh, I'm Millie's friend,
David. Is she here?

859
01:03:09,619 --> 01:03:11,348
Last I checked she was with you.

860
01:03:12,722 --> 01:03:14,952
Hey. Your friend came by.

861
01:03:16,692 --> 01:03:20,423
- What are you talking about?
- Black guy, white hair. You just missed him.

862
01:03:38,581 --> 01:03:40,378
[Beeping]

863
01:03:41,484 --> 01:03:43,452
[Line Ringing]

864
01:03:47,390 --> 01:03:50,052
<i>[Phone Ringing]</i>

865
01:03:50,159 --> 01:03:52,127
<i>[Ringing Continues]</i>

866
01:03:53,296 --> 01:03:55,196
[Gasps]

867
01:03:55,298 --> 01:03:57,926
- Jesus.
- Hey.

868
01:03:58,034 --> 01:03:59,934
<i>David, wh-</i>

869
01:04:01,037 --> 01:04:03,062
What the hell are you doing here?

870
01:04:03,172 --> 01:04:05,402
I buzzed, but you didn't pick up.

871
01:04:05,508 --> 01:04:09,342
- So you just broke in?
- Yeah. Well, I needed to
make sure that you were okay.

872
01:04:09,445 --> 01:04:13,006
<i>No, David. I'm not okay.</i>
<i>I got left in an airport in Rome.</i>

873
01:04:13,115 --> 01:04:15,583
[Exhales Deeply]

874
01:04:15,685 --> 01:04:17,653
I'm sorry.

875
01:04:20,089 --> 01:04:22,023
You're sorry.

876
01:04:22,124 --> 01:04:24,024
Thank you.

877
01:04:27,496 --> 01:04:29,464
I think you should leave.

878
01:04:33,769 --> 01:04:36,704
<i>[Car Doors Opening, Closing]</i>

879
01:04:36,806 --> 01:04:38,706
<i>David, you need to leave!</i>

880
01:04:38,808 --> 01:04:41,675
<i>[Roland] Come on. Snap to it.</i>
<i>We don't have much time.</i>

881
01:04:41,777 --> 01:04:44,041
- What? What are you doing?
- Uh-

882
01:04:44,146 --> 01:04:47,047
- David, I told you to leave.
- Uh-

883
01:04:47,149 --> 01:04:49,549
- <i>Um-</i>
- "Um" what?

884
01:04:49,652 --> 01:04:53,850
- I'm not in banking, okay?
- No, really?

885
01:04:53,956 --> 01:04:56,584
- I mean, the money did come
from a bank, you know.
- Yeah.

886
01:04:56,692 --> 01:05:01,629
- Uh, a few banks, actually.
- Are-Are you telling me you're a bank robber?

887
01:05:01,731 --> 01:05:03,699
Small part. Uh-

888
01:05:05,368 --> 01:05:08,030
Will you please get out of my house?

889
01:05:09,338 --> 01:05:11,306
[Gasps]

890
01:05:16,746 --> 01:05:18,111
Uh-huh.

891
01:05:19,348 --> 01:05:21,612
- [Screams]
- Millie, I'm sorry.

892
01:05:21,717 --> 01:05:24,151
Wh- Oh, my God. Okay.

893
01:05:24,253 --> 01:05:26,721
- <i>I'm really sorry, but we gotta go.</i>
- Just go. Leave me alone.

894
01:05:26,822 --> 01:05:29,120
Come on.

895
01:05:29,225 --> 01:05:30,886
This might hurt a little bit, okay?

896
01:05:30,993 --> 01:05:34,485
- [Grunts]
- [Screams]

897
01:05:34,597 --> 01:05:37,293
- It's okay.
- Where am I?

898
01:05:37,400 --> 01:05:40,130
Trust me, okay?
[Echoing]

899
01:05:40,236 --> 01:05:42,431
- I'm not gonna hurt you.
- Don't you even come near me.

900
01:05:42,538 --> 01:05:44,563
- Millie.
- Don't even come near me.

901
01:05:48,277 --> 01:05:50,768
I'm gonna explain this, all right?
I'm gonna explain everything.

902
01:05:53,950 --> 01:05:55,918
In here.

903
01:05:56,018 --> 01:05:58,953
Just, uh-Just stay where you are, all right?
Just stay right there.

904
01:05:59,055 --> 01:06:01,649
- David?
- [Roland] Hurry up. It's closing.

905
01:06:14,804 --> 01:06:16,704
[Groans]

906
01:06:21,811 --> 01:06:24,473
<i>Griffin.</i>

907
01:06:24,580 --> 01:06:26,605
There's something I gotta tell ya.

908
01:06:26,716 --> 01:06:29,014
- Did you find her?
- There's something that's gonna piss you off.

909
01:06:29,118 --> 01:06:31,552
- Piss me off?
- David.

910
01:06:31,654 --> 01:06:33,713
What is this?

911
01:06:33,823 --> 01:06:35,552
- David?
- What's she doing here?

912
01:06:35,658 --> 01:06:38,149
- This isn't some kind of clubhouse, you know.
- <i>What is going on?</i>

913
01:06:38,260 --> 01:06:39,852
- <i>Stay inside.</i>
- Wanna see the top of Everest?

914
01:06:39,962 --> 01:06:42,055
- I was trying to tell you.
- Maybe the bottom?

915
01:06:42,164 --> 01:06:44,223
- What?
- Griffin, listen to me. l-

916
01:06:44,333 --> 01:06:46,233
That's what I was
trying to tell you.

917
01:06:46,335 --> 01:06:48,633
By bringing her down here, they can
follow you. They have a machine.

918
01:06:48,738 --> 01:06:51,468
- It can open wormholes and keep them open.
- What are you talking about?

919
01:06:51,574 --> 01:06:53,166
I'm saying they can
